-- title:
--   A common level-stable chart dominating the ends of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which (`hH₁`) is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which (`hK`) is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the field generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ exhibiting $L$ as its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series equal to the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral }j\text{-numerator series})$ of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A K j` over the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with the canonical morphism $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}} : \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the Drinfeld-chart witness at every supersingular point of the special fibre. It asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$, $v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{X,z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$$
--   from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$, such that, writing `toC` for the map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the canonical germ map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ coming from $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, the following seven clauses hold. First, $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$. Second, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ acts on ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ as the slash action of the matrix attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ by `conjElemN q`, read through any $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$ — the subalgebra $C$ is $\tau$-stable. Third, for such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ and such $\tau$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$. Fourth, for such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ whose restriction to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ conjugating the composite $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ into the corresponding composite for $\tau$; $\theta$ fixing the classes of constants; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$; $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$. Fifth, a separation of branches: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing some element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct. Sixth, for a prime $P$ of $S$ subject to the same three conditions with tangent form $X_0$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$. Seventh, a Hasse rider: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $q$-expansion of $j$ with the variable raised to the $q$-th power, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \geq 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W$, not both in the maximal ideal, with $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, the value $\sum_{i \le e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ of the degree-$e_0$ form of $h$ is a unit, and $e$ carries the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   Now fix such data at one point: a point $z$ of $X$, an element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk as above lying in its maximal ideal, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`), with $y'$ the ideal $y$ (`hy'y`); and fix one witness $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ for this point, the hypothesis `hW₁` being exactly the conjunction of the seven clauses listed above for these data.
--
--   Let $J$ be the ideal of $C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form
--   $$(\tau|_C)^{-1}\Bigl( (e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY})^{-1}\bigl(\text{the ideal of } S \text{ generated by the classes of } C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ X_0,\ X_1 \bigr)\Bigr),$$
--   $\gamma$ running over the elements of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ as above which preserve $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by the set of $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$, that is, $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ (the letter is reused; here it is a valuation subring of $K$) containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypotheses on $B$ and $W$ are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h$ outside the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses) describes the special fibre of $B$. For every algebra structure of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld equation, whose kernel consists of the elements lying in the maximal ideal of $W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is a unit $c$ of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma), c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(M,c) \mapsto \det(M)\,c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}(\gamma,c) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$. Further, $B$ is stable under every level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$, in the sense that $\tau$ carries all elements of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$ into that prime; an element of $B$ all of whose level translates by $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $W$ as soon as it preserves $y$ on $C$.
--
--   Finally, let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised (`hends`) as follows: a subring $O$ belongs to it precisely when there is a nonzero $a \in J$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a := C[\{x \in K : xa \in J\}]$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (an $f \in K$ lies in $O$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$), every element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $O$ does not contain $B$. The hypothesis `hperm` states that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserves $W$, every $O \in$ `ends` is carried by $\tau$ into some $O' \in$ `ends`, in the sense that $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$ such that: $B_c$ is of finite type over $A$; $B_c$ is stable under every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and for every $O \in$ `ends`, first $B_c \subseteq O$, and second an element $f \in K$ lies in $O$ if and only if there are $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ invertible in $O$ and $fh = g$, so that each end is the localisation of the single chart $B_c$ at the elements of $B_c$ that are units there.
--
--   This is a step in the analysis of the ends of the blown-up supersingular chart of an integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, in the variant frame where full auxiliary level at $q$ is replaced by a diamond condition at a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, so that the argument applies for all primes $q$. It produces one finite-type $A$-chart, stable under the level automorphisms coming from $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, which dominates all the ends simultaneously and has each end as a localisation; it is used by the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_and_stabilizer_and_valuativeCover_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_and_stabilizer_and_valuativeCover_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
